sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant API as API Controller
    participant Mediator as MediatR pipeline<br/>(ValidationBehavior)
    box rgb(241,243,234) Handler Layer
        participant RegHandler as RegisterUserHandler
        participant UserMgr as UserManager(ApplicationUser)
        participant TokenSvc as TokenService
    end
    box rgb(235,236,227) Infrastructure Layer
        participant Argon2 as Argon2PasswordHasher
        participant JWT as JWT Infrastructure
        participant SMTP as Email Provider
        participant Template as Template Provider
    end
    box rgb(219,238,221) Repository / Cross-slice
        participant UserStore as DapperUserStore<br/>(IUserStore/IUserPasswordStore/IUserEmailStore)
        participant ProfileHandler as CreateUserProfileHandler<br/>(Profile slice)
        participant EmailDispatcher as EmailDispatcher<br/>(Features.Emails)
    end
    participant DB as SQL Server

    Note over UserMgr: ASP.NET Core Identity's UserManager replaces the deleted AuthRepository — handlers delegate to UserManager, which calls DapperUserStore (persistence) and Argon2PasswordHasher.

    User->>API: POST /api/auth/register {username, firstName, lastName, email, dateOfBirth, password}
    activate API
    API->>Mediator: Send(RegisterUserCommand)
    activate Mediator
    Note right of Mediator: ValidationBehavior runs RegisterUserValidator — username 3-64 chars alphanumeric+[._-], valid email ≤128 chars, password min 8 chars with upper/lower/number/special, DateOfBirth 19+ years old

    alt Validation fails
        Mediator->>API: throws FluentValidation.ValidationException
        API->>User: 400 Bad Request {message, errors}
    else Validation succeeds
        Mediator->>RegHandler: Handle(command)
        activate RegHandler
        RegHandler->>RegHandler: user = new UserAccount{...}.ToApplicationUser()

        RegHandler->>UserMgr: CreateAsync(user, password)
        activate UserMgr
        UserMgr->>Argon2: HashPassword(user, password)
        activate Argon2
        Note right of Argon2: Argon2id — salt 16 bytes, memory 64MB, iterations 4, parallelism 2 (fixed, to avoid thread-pool exhaustion), hash output 32 bytes
        Argon2-->>UserMgr: PHC string in Argon2id format (algorithm, version, memory/time/parallelism params, salt, hash)
        deactivate Argon2

        UserMgr->>UserStore: SetPasswordHashAsync(user, hash)
        Note right of UserStore: user.Id is still empty here — only sets the in-memory hash — CreateAsync writes it to UserCredential itself

        UserMgr->>UserStore: FindByNameAsync(username)
        activate UserStore
        UserStore->>DB: SELECT ... FROM UserAccount WHERE Username = @Username
        activate DB
        DB-->>UserStore: null (user doesn't exist)
        deactivate DB
        deactivate UserStore

        UserMgr->>UserStore: FindByEmailAsync(email)
        activate UserStore
        UserStore->>DB: SELECT ... FROM UserAccount WHERE Email = @Email
        activate DB
        DB-->>UserStore: null (email doesn't exist)
        deactivate DB
        deactivate UserStore
        Note right of UserMgr: Default UserManager validators check uniqueness before CreateAsync — DapperUserStore.CreateAsync also guards a genuine race via a caught duplicate-key SqlException (2601/2627)

        UserMgr->>UserStore: CreateAsync(user)
        activate UserStore
        UserStore->>DB: BEGIN TRANSACTION
        activate DB
        UserStore->>DB: INSERT INTO UserAccount (...) OUTPUT INSERTED.UserAccountID
        DB-->>UserStore: UserAccountId (GUID)
        UserStore->>DB: INSERT INTO UserCredential (UserAccountId, Hash)
        UserStore->>DB: COMMIT TRANSACTION
        deactivate DB
        Note right of UserStore: Both statements run via Dapper against a single DbTransaction, not a stored procedure

        UserStore-->>UserMgr: IdentityResult.Success (user.Id set)
        deactivate UserStore
        UserMgr-->>RegHandler: IdentityResult
        deactivate UserMgr

        alt !result.Succeeded
            RegHandler->>Mediator: throw ConflictException (DuplicateUserName/DuplicateEmail → "Username or email already exists", otherwise joined error descriptions)
            Mediator->>API: propagate
            API->>User: 409 Conflict "Username or email already exists"
        else result.Succeeded
            RegHandler->>Mediator: Send(CreateUserProfileCommand(user.Id, ""))
            activate Mediator
            Mediator->>ProfileHandler: Handle(command)
            activate ProfileHandler
            ProfileHandler->>DB: INSERT INTO UserProfile (UserAccountId, Biography)
            activate DB
            DB-->>ProfileHandler: UserProfileId
            deactivate DB
            ProfileHandler-->>Mediator: UserProfileId
            deactivate ProfileHandler
            Mediator-->>RegHandler: UserProfileId
            deactivate Mediator

            RegHandler->>TokenSvc: GenerateAccessToken(user)
            activate TokenSvc
            TokenSvc->>JWT: GenerateJwt(userId, username, expiry)
            activate JWT
            Note right of JWT: HS256, expires 1 hour, claims sub/unique_name/iat/jti
            JWT->>JWT: Create JWT with claims, sign with secret key
            JWT-->>TokenSvc: Access Token
            deactivate JWT
            TokenSvc-->>RegHandler: Access Token
            deactivate TokenSvc

            RegHandler->>TokenSvc: GenerateRefreshToken(user)
            activate TokenSvc
            TokenSvc->>JWT: GenerateJwt(userId, username, expiry)
            activate JWT
            Note right of JWT: Expires 21 days (504h), same structure as access token, signed with a separate secret
            JWT-->>TokenSvc: Refresh Token
            deactivate JWT
            TokenSvc-->>RegHandler: Refresh Token
            deactivate TokenSvc

            RegHandler->>TokenSvc: GenerateConfirmationToken(user)
            activate TokenSvc
            TokenSvc->>JWT: GenerateJwt(userId, username, expiry)
            activate JWT
            Note right of JWT: Expires 30 minutes, signed with a third, separate secret
            JWT-->>TokenSvc: Confirmation Token
            deactivate JWT
            TokenSvc-->>RegHandler: Confirmation Token
            deactivate TokenSvc

            RegHandler->>Mediator: Send(SendRegistrationEmailCommand) (Shared.Application cross-slice contract)
            activate Mediator
            Note right of Mediator: Routed to Features.Emails' SendRegistrationEmailHandler — the second of two cross-slice dispatches in this flow (profile creation is the first)
            Mediator->>EmailDispatcher: SendRegistrationEmailAsync(firstName, email, confirmationToken)
            activate EmailDispatcher

            EmailDispatcher->>Template: RenderUserRegisteredEmailAsync(firstName, confirmationLink)
            activate Template
            Note right of Template: Razor component — header/branding, welcome message, confirmation button, footer
            Template->>Template: Render Razor component to HTML
            Template-->>EmailDispatcher: HTML email content
            deactivate Template

            EmailDispatcher->>SMTP: SendAsync(email, subject, body)
            activate SMTP
            Note right of SMTP: MailKit — host/port from SMTP_HOST/SMTP_PORT, StartTLS when SMTP_USE_SSL=true, optional username/password auth
            SMTP->>SMTP: Build MIME message, connect, authenticate, send, disconnect
            SMTP-->>EmailDispatcher: Success / throws
            deactivate SMTP
            deactivate EmailDispatcher
            deactivate Mediator

            alt Email sent successfully
                RegHandler->>RegHandler: emailSent = true
            else mediator.Send throws
                RegHandler->>RegHandler: catch(Exception), log to stderr, emailSent = false
            end

            RegHandler-->>Mediator: RegistrationPayload(userAccountId, username, refreshToken, accessToken, confirmationEmailSent)
            deactivate RegHandler
            Mediator-->>API: RegistrationPayload
            deactivate Mediator
            API->>User: 201 Created {message: "User registered successfully.", payload: {...}}
        end
    end
    deactivate API
